  "_about": "USAF T.O. 1C-130A-2-2, page 1-3: the C-130A Hercules (late, radome nose) three-view, a Wikimedia Commons scan (File:Lockheed C-130A Hercules (late) 3-view line drawing.png, 1797 x 2566 px, public domain). The side view: layers.py --mode image --threshold 170 at scale 3 (3 raster px per scan px), clip 330,1960,1797,2566 (scan px). Pixels of that raster, line centres. The nacelle and the wing over the top of the fuselage hide the crown from the propeller to behind the wing (bridged); the main gear's sponson and wheels hide the belly between them (bridged). Both nacelles a side are drawn, the outboard one higher by the dihedral: engine is the inboard one (its top hidden behind the outboard nacelle, placed 28 px under the outboard's: free points), engine2 the outboard.",
